Package: monocombo
Title: Mono-Combo Seamless Clinical Trial Design, Simulation, and Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Bo", "Zhang",
    email = "bo.zhang@uth.tmc.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a unified framework for designing, simulating operating
    characteristics of, and analyzing multi-arm multi-stage (MAMS) seamless
    clinical trials that start with monotherapy and roll in combination therapy
    mid-trial when needed. Supports binary endpoints and four design flavors:
    OR-Platform (order-restricted), Platform, 2-stage MAMS, and 3-stage MAMS.
    Implements group-sequential efficacy and futility boundaries using O'Brien-
    Fleming or Pocock alpha-spending, with strong control of the one-sided
    family-wise error rate (FWER) via Dunnett-type multivariate normal/t
    probability calculations.
